================================================================================
EXPERIMENT LEDGER (runs driven by this module, 2026-08-03; all identities exact,
all failures are search/transport negatives -- NEVER infeasibility evidence,
THM-3029 sec 1)
================================================================================
BAND PROFILES (max_j |E[j][dt_j - m]| / cap, one-level differenced carve):
  32-> 64 (CLOSED, 0 fallbacks): m=0: 3      m=2: 1.47   m>=4: <=1.2
  16-> 32 (CLOSED, 22 fallbacks): m=0: 7     m=4: 5.3    m=12: 2.9
  64->128 from beam seed:        m=0: 21    m=20: 16.6  m=40: 11.3  <- disease
  64->128 low-k: k=0: 29  k=1..12: 13-17 (rows 22-26, 63-67)
ROW LOADS L1(E_j)/2^dt_j, 64->128 beam seed: hot rows (4: 6.0) (22-26: 4.3-4.8)
  (45-46: 4.6-5.5) (57: 7.3) (76-77: 9.1/6.1) (84-85: 6.0/5.5); sum = 236.2
CARRY AVALANCHE LAW (measured, debug_fallback): a bulge at depth m climbs
  exactly 1 depth/row (lift edge C(r2,.), r2 = dt[j+1]-dt[j]+1) growing
  x2-4/row; caps at fixed small depth grow only ~x1.5 -> any band bulge
  above box scale is terminal within ~m rows.  First fallback (beam seed,
  bandvac 29/4/keep1, W=12 L=24): row 20 depth 12, |e|/cap = 6.7e5; death
  row 32.  EXCHANGE RATES: forward transport multiplies mass 2^r vs cap
  growth 2^(0.6r) (net loss 2^(0.4r) ~ 2^(row) per row); backward gather
  divides mass 2^(1.6dj) vs caps 2^(0.6dj) but splash C(r,t) loses beyond
  depth ~d/4.  Top cells (k = d_i) admit NO move in either direction.
STEER SELF-CORRECTION (measured): local E edits at prescribed cells are
  re-planned around -- identical overflow e = -99 vs cap 97 at (35,96)
  after every donor variant; the only live dials are the +-1 top targets.
SWEEP GRIDS 64->128 (Steer engine): raw + bandvac + vacuum_fix + teleport
  (nearest-first, r<=24) x W in {10..100} x L in {8..40}: all fail rows
  12-65 (band bulges).  32x4 (T=3 double-fold carve, overshoot 5739):
  raw W=40 L=40: 'final carry nonzero' (all 128 rows threaded); vac W=10
  L=8: nfall=1 (single e=-99 overflow) then top -3 at row 36 -- the
  closest deterministic approach.  sweep_beam (top-sign branching, exact
  per-state Steer override; reproduces 32->64 with nfall=0): 32x4vac dies
  row 46.
CONCLUSION: seed cell fatness is NOT the 64->128 obstruction (carve
  overshoot 29 vs 25 at the closed 32->64).  The obstruction is the
  near-top BAND of the carve, inherited from the seed witnesses'
  correction windows touching the top cells of rows ~30-50.  The needed
  object is an R=64 witness whose corrections avoid the top band (depth
  <~ 45); hunt-slim (rank = Bernstein-cell roughness of the residual) is
  implemented here as the follow-up search.
