solve_prof(R=64, floor, beam=120, ctrl=2, span=2, rank='cellmax'
  = (residual degree, max |Bernstein cell| of residual at own degree)):
  SOLVED in 32s, verified exact -> amm12592_floor_witness_R64_cellslim.json
  mid max|c| = 3.22e13  (beam-l1deg seed: 3.7e18; doubling output: 3.4e21)
  -- five orders slimmer, at the F_64 ~ 1.6e13 coefficient scale.
  carve 64->128 overshoot: 19  (< 25 of the CLOSED 32->64 step!)
  carve tops: +-1..9 (16->32-closed-like); band m<=20: 7-9x; m=30: 3.2x.
  band_vacuum(M0=29, spread=4) on this carve: ZERO stuck cells (fully
  clean band to depth 29 -- first time on any 64->128 carve).
REMAINING OBSTRUCTION (the R=128 frontier, isolated): stuck band mass at
  depths 30-45 in rows ~17-40, total ~7.0e23 -- SEED-INDEPENDENT (same
  7.0-7.1e23 for beam-l1deg, cellmax, cellsat seeds): an intrinsic
  component of the differenced-carve transport, not of the seed.  Both
  transport directions lose exponentially there (forward 2^r mass vs
  2^(0.6r) caps; backward splash C(r,t) vs cap growth (d-m)/m < 3 beyond
  depth ~d/4), and the early rows' total capacity is genuinely too small
  to absorb it.  Sweeps die at rows 33-36 when its climbing tail reaches
  the top band.  NEXT LEVERS: (i) in-row cancellation routing against
  opposite-signed bulk (row loads L1/2^d up to 9 mean heavy cancellation
  is available in principle); (ii) a carve variant that avoids creating
  the 7e23 band component (different pairing/differencing of THM-3026
  products); (iii) direct R=128 beam with rank='cellmax' -- the rank that
  produced the 5-orders-slimmer R=64 witness in 32 seconds.
